        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute Kirchhoff stress and algorithmic tangent using automatic differentiation. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This method overrides <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_1af123a7f01a7534862ec08e82fcc0a443" kindref="member">MaterialFiniteStrain::computeStress()</ref> and provides a generic AD-based implementation for finite strain material models.</para>
<para>The child class must implement <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_a_d_1a1f54b4133455a51f197dc3793866e082" kindref="member">computeStressAD()</ref>, which evaluates the constitutive response (Kirchhoff stress and any state updates) for a dual-valued deformation gradient. This base implementation then uses Marmot::Math::Differentiation::Automatic::dF_dT() to:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>compute the Kirchhoff stress <formula id="32">$\boldsymbol{\tau}$</formula> for the given deformation, and</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>compute the consistent algorithmic tangent <formula id="35">$\partial \boldsymbol{\tau} / \partial \boldsymbol{F}$</formula>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Automatic differentiation requires multiple seeded evaluations of <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_a_d_1a1f54b4133455a51f197dc3793866e082" kindref="member">computeStressAD()</ref>. Therefore, the state variables are reset to their &quot;old&quot; values before each seeded call. Implementations of <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_a_d_1a1f54b4133455a51f197dc3793866e082" kindref="member">computeStressAD()</ref> must update state based only on primal values of the dual inputs and must not branch or accumulate history based on derivative components.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">response</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Constitutive response container (stress, density, energy, state variables). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">tangents</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Algorithmic moduli container; filled with <formula id="36">$\partial \tau / \partial F$</formula>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">deformation</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_1_1_deformation" kindref="compound">Deformation</ref> state (deformation gradient <formula id="23">$\boldsymbol{F}$</formula>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">timeIncrement</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Time increment information for rate-/history-dependent models. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
