        <type>void</type>
        <definition>virtual void Marmot::Materials::MaterialFiniteStrainAD::computeStressAD</definition>
        <argsstring>(ConstitutiveResponseAD&lt; 3 &gt; &amp;response, const DeformationAD&lt; 3 &gt; &amp;deformation, const TimeIncrement &amp;timeIncrement) const =0</argsstring>
        <name>computeStressAD</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::Materials::MaterialFiniteStrainAD::computeStressAD</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_a_d_1_1_constitutive_response_a_d" kindref="compound">ConstitutiveResponseAD</ref>&lt; 3 &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>response</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_a_d_1_1_deformation_a_d" kindref="compound">DeformationAD</ref>&lt; 3 &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>deformation</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_1_1_time_increment" kindref="compound">TimeIncrement</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>timeIncrement</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute the constitutive response in automatic differentiation (AD) form. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This pure virtual function must be implemented by derived material models to compute the Kirchhoff stress tensor in <computeroutput>response.tau</computeroutput> for a given deformation in dual number form. The base class uses this AD formulation together with Marmot::Math::Differentiation::Automatic utilities to obtain algorithmic tangents by differentiating the stress with respect to the deformation gradient.</para>
<para>Implementations may update the provided state variables via <computeroutput>response.stateVars</computeroutput> according to the given time increment.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">response</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Constitutive response in AD form (3D), with <computeroutput>response.tau</computeroutput> to be filled with the computed Kirchhoff stress. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">deformation</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_finite_strain_1_1_deformation" kindref="compound">Deformation</ref> state in AD form (3D), providing the deformation gradient <formula id="23">$\boldsymbol{F}$</formula> as dual numbers. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">timeIncrement</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Current time increment information for the constitutive update. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
